    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d407">

                <pb facs="0454" n="420" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg420"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Mr. Lewis Baker.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-11-03"><hi rendition="#italic">November 3,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 618.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatches Nos. 852 and 857, dated, respectively, the 12th and 18th ultimo, both
                    relating to the award of Gen. E. P. Alexander,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d407-f1"/>
                    the engineer arbitrator of the commissions of limits of Costa Rica and
                    Nicaragua. The first-named dispatch states that great satisfaction has been
                    expressed in Nicaragua over the decision, and the latter transmits a copy of the
                    award.</p>
                <p>In this connection I inclose herewith for your information a copy of a note,
                    dated the 29th ultimo, from the Costa Rican minister at this capital announcing
                    that his Government has accepted the award.</p>
                <p>You will report to the Department as early as possible whether Nicaragua also
                    accepts.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Sherman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
